If I had the choice of inviting historical characters for a dinner party and having an insightful conversation with them, I would choose the following people:

1. Thomas Jefferson - one of the Founding Fathers of the United States and author of the Declaration of Independence;
2. Marie Curie - a pioneering scientist whose work on radioactivity helped to revolutionize the medical field;
3. Abraham Lincoln - a significant leader during the American Civil War and known for his efforts to abolish slavery;
4. Martin Luther King Jr. - a prominent civil rights activist who fought against racial discrimination in the US;
5. Albert Einstein - a theoretical physicist known for his contributions to the development of modern physics and his famous equation E=mc².

These individuals were not only key leaders in their respective fields but also made substantial contributions to humanity throughout history. Their insights, experiences, and perspectives would provide fascinating stories and discussions that could shed light on various issues faced by society at that time.

